==Old English==

===Etymology===
Common Germanic: cognate with Old Saxon [[skakan]], Old Norse [[skaka]].

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|/'ʃacan/}}

===Intransitive verb===
{{rfc-trverb|Intransitive verb}}
'''scacan''' (Class VI strong)

# to [[pass]] or [[depart]]
# to [[quiver]] or [[vibrate]]

===Transitive verb===
'''scacan''' (Class VI strong)

# to [[flourish]] or [[wave]] (an object)
# to cause something to [[quiver]], [[flutter]], or [[shake]]

